{
  "nbformat": 4,
  "nbformat_minor": 5,
  "metadata": {
    "kernelspec": {
      "name": "maxima",
      "display_name": "Maxima",
      "language": "maxima"
    },
    "aximar": {}
  },
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "# Sequences and Limits\n\nA sequence $(a_n)_{n \\in \\mathbb{N}}$ **converges to** $L$ — written $a_n \\to L$ — if for every $\\varepsilon > 0$ there exists $N$ such that\n\n$$n \\ge N \\;\\Longrightarrow\\; |a_n - L| < \\varepsilon.$$\n\nRead aloud: *no matter how thin a window of width $\\varepsilon$ you draw around $L$, the sequence eventually stays inside that window forever.* This is the foundational definition of analysis — limits of functions, derivatives, integrals, and series all reduce to it.\n\nThis notebook makes the definition concrete: for a given sequence and $\\varepsilon$, we find the actual $N$ and visualise the \"tail-in-the-window\" property.\n",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "load(\"numerics\")$\nload(\"ax-plots\")$",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 43,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## A textbook convergent sequence\n\nTake $a_n = 1 + \\dfrac{1}{n}$. The limit is $L = 1$. Pick $\\varepsilon = 0.05$ and find the smallest $N$ such that all later terms lie in $(L - \\varepsilon, L + \\varepsilon)$.\n",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "seq_a(n) := 1 + 1/n$\nL_a : 1.0$\neps : 0.05$\n\nn_max : 80$\nn_vals : makelist(n, n, 1, n_max)$\na_vals : map(lambda([n], float(seq_a(n))), n_vals)$\n\n/* Find smallest N with |a_n - L| < eps for all n ≥ N */\nN_min : 1$\nfor n : 1 thru n_max do\n  if abs(a_vals[n] - L_a) >= eps then N_min : n + 1$\nprint(\"Smallest N for ε =\", eps, \"is N =\", N_min)$\nprint(\"Closed-form check: 1/N < eps  ⇒  N > 1/eps =\", 1.0 / eps)$",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 44,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "Smallest N for ε = 0.05 is N = 21\nClosed-form check: 1/N < eps  ⇒  N > 1/eps = 20.0"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Visualise the tail-in-the-window\n\nPlot $a_n$ as discrete points; overlay the band $(L - \\varepsilon, L + \\varepsilon)$ and mark $N$. Every dot to the right of $N$ falls inside the band — that's literally what convergence means.\n",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "ax_draw2d(\n  color=\"blue\", marker_size=4, name=\"a_n = 1 + 1/n\",\n  points(n_vals, a_vals),\n  color=\"black\", dash=\"dash\", name=\"L = 1\",\n  explicit(L_a, t, 0, n_max),\n  color=\"red\", dash=\"dot\", name=\"L ± ε\",\n  explicit(L_a + eps, t, 0, n_max),\n  color=\"red\", dash=\"dot\",\n  explicit(L_a - eps, t, 0, n_max),\n  color=\"green\", line_width=2, name=\"N (smallest)\",\n  points([N_min, N_min], [L_a - eps, L_a + eps]),\n  title=\"Convergence: every term beyond N stays in the ε-band\",\n  xlabel=\"n\", ylabel=\"a_n\",\n  grid=true, showlegend=true\n)$",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 45,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "data": {
